          "name": "pqs:context",
          "value": "This is a blockchain-related cryptocurrency signing implementation using the secp256k1 elliptic curve. The code is actively creating cryptographic contexts and performing signature operations. While secp256k1 is not directly vulnerable to quantum attacks in the same way as RSA or ECDH, it is classified as a classical signature algorithm that will need migration to post-quantum alternatives like ML-DSA."
